      "content": "The end function"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Similar to begin(), we also have the end() function, which returns an iterator to the element one past the last element."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "auto iter = number.end();"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here, iter points to the element one past the element. This can be useful to access the last element of the container or to iterate through the container in reverse."
    },
